# ShellCheck config for the test suites in this directory only (#209). The
# shipped scripts one level up get no blanket disables.
#
# These checks flag the harness idioms every suite is written in, where the
# flagged behaviour is the intended one:
#   SC2015  `[ cond ] && ok || fail "..."`: ok only bumps a counter and cannot
#           fail, so fail never runs after a true condition.
#   SC2016  single-quoted jq/awk/node programs and literal `$var` text in
#           fixtures and expected output, which must not expand.
#   SC2181  `cmd; [ $? -ne 0 ]; ok ... $?`: the exit code is itself the thing
#           under test, recorded before the next assertion.
#   SC2319  `[ cond ]; ok "..." $?`: $? of the condition is the result that ok
#           records, which is exactly what this warning says it refers to.
disable=SC2015,SC2016,SC2181,SC2319
